1171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 434 0 R
/E (As part of the 2008 initiative, Hester Street published a study and recommendations report that explicitly identified the Delancey Street comfort station as a strong candidate for reuse as a community space. In subsequent years, Hester Street also led several temporary art installations in the pedestrian malls, most notably in 2010 in collaboration with NYC DOT, to activate the area before and during capital improvements.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 434 0 R
/E (In 2011, approximately $1 million in funding was allocated by the Lower Manhattan Development Corporation for the renovation of the abandoned comfort station at Delancey. Hester Street advocated for this allocation; however, the funding appears to have been absorbed into Parks Department processes, and no renovation work ultimately occurred at the site. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1173 0 obj
<<
